-- title:
--   Dimension bound for the Witt-coordinate subalgebra of a finite F,V-stable subgroup
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$, with $p$ prime, and let $C$ be a commutative ring equipped with a $k$-bialgebra structure. For each $n$, [`Deformation.wittHom k p n C`](def/Dieudonne_WittVectorHom.html#L246) denotes the additive subgroup of `TruncatedWittVector p n C` consisting of those $x$ with $W_n(\Delta)(x) = W_n(\iota_1)(x) + W_n(\iota_2)(x)$, where $\Delta$ is the comultiplication of $C$ and $\iota_1,\iota_2 : C \to C \otimes_k C$ are the two inclusions; [`Deformation.DieudonneModule k p C`](def/Dieudonne_WittHomColimit.html#L234) is the direct limit of these groups along the shift maps $W_n \to W_m$ for $n \le m$, with [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.of k p C n`](def/Dieudonne_WittHomColimit.html#L245) the canonical map from level $n$, and with the additive endomorphisms `frobenius` and `verschiebung` induced levelwise by the coordinatewise Frobenius and by the coordinate shift. Let $N$ be a finite additive subgroup of [`Deformation.DieudonneModule k p C`](def/Dieudonne_WittHomColimit.html#L234) that is carried into itself by `frobenius` and by `verschiebung`. Let $S \subseteq C$ be the set of elements $c$ for which there are $n$, an element $x$ of [`Deformation.wittHom k p n C`](def/Dieudonne_WittVectorHom.html#L246) whose class in the Dieudonné module lies in $N$, and an index $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\ n$ with $i$-th Witt coordinate of $x$ equal to $c$. Then the $k$-subalgebra `Algebra.adjoin k S` of $C$ is a finite $k$-module and its $k$-dimension is at most $\mathrm{Nat.card}\, N$.
--
--   This is the counting half of the comparison between the order of a finite commutative group scheme and the cardinality of its Dieudonné module: the subalgebra generated by the Witt coordinates of the homomorphisms occurring in $N$ is the coordinate ring of the schematic image of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ in a product of Witt groups, and the bound reads as an inequality of orders. It is used in the project's results on the Dieudonné module of a Cartier dual over a local ring and on the Witt kernel subgroup.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_DieudonneModule_finrank_adjoin_coeff_le_natCard.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Dieudonne_DatumAndHonda
import Definitions.Def_Dieudonne_WittVectorHom
import Definitions.Def_Dieudonne_WittHomColimit

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u v

theorem Deformation.DieudonneModule.finrank_adjoin_coeff_le_natCard
    (k : Type u) [Field k] (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] [CharP k p]
    (C : Type v) [CommRing C] [Bialgebra k C]
    (N : AddSubgroup (Deformation.DieudonneModule k p C)) [Finite N]
    (hF : ∀ z ∈ N, Deformation.DieudonneModule.frobenius k p C z ∈ N)
    (hV : ∀ z ∈ N, Deformation.DieudonneModule.verschiebung k p C z ∈ N) :
    Module.Finite k ↥(Algebra.adjoin k {c : C | ∃ (n : ℕ) (x : Deformation.wittHom k p n C) (i : Fin n),
        Deformation.DieudonneModule.of k p C n x ∈ N ∧ (x : TruncatedWittVector p n C).coeff i = c}) ∧
      Module.finrank k ↥(Algebra.adjoin k {c : C | ∃ (n : ℕ) (x : Deformation.wittHom k p n C) (i : Fin n),
        Deformation.DieudonneModule.of k p C n x ∈ N ∧ (x : TruncatedWittVector p n C).coeff i = c}) ≤
      Nat.card N := by sorry
